# v1.17: the Trash in Files. Delete moves a note to the trash; a Trash button
# appears beside New note and New folder while it holds something; the Trash
# lists what was deleted (folder and how long ago), a tap selects a note,
# Restore puts it back (under a free name if its path was taken), and Empty
# trash (two taps) removes everything for good.
# Run: `scripts/sim.sh --headless tests/emu/v1.17-trash.script docs/screenshots/v1.17`.
expect-open field-notes.md
tap-on Files
shot v1.17-files-no-trash
tap-on drafts
tap-on More:chapter-01.md
tap-on Delete
tap-on Delete
expect-no-file drafts/chapter-01.md
shot v1.17-files-with-trash
tap-on Up
tap-on More:scratch.txt
tap-on Delete
tap-on Delete
expect-no-file scratch.txt
# Make the two look like they were deleted at different times.
age-trash 1 200000
age-trash 0 7500
tap-on Trash
shot v1.17-trash
# Restore with nothing selected says what to do.
tap-on Restore
shot v1.17-trash-nothing-selected
tap-on scratch.txt
shot v1.17-trash-selected
tap-on Restore
expect-file scratch.txt
shot v1.17-trash-restored
# The last item: Restore, and the sheet leaves the Trash by itself.
tap-on chapter-01.md
tap-on Restore
expect-file drafts/chapter-01.md
# Nothing left: back in Files, no Trash button.
shot v1.17-files-after-restore
# Delete again, then empty the trash with two taps.
tap-on drafts
tap-on More:chapter-01.md
tap-on Delete
tap-on Delete
tap-on Up
tap-on Trash
tap-on Empty trash
shot v1.17-empty-armed
tap-on Empty trash
shot v1.17-emptied
expect-no-file .trash
expect-no-file drafts/chapter-01.md
